WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
Imagine a ladder.

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.000
The top is 10,
representing the best possible life you can have.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.000
The bottom is 0,
the worst possible life.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Which step of the ladder do you think you are on?

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.415
7.

00:00:09.415 --> 00:00:10.213
Maybe 8.

00:00:10.213 --> 00:00:11.063
Probably 6 or 7.

00:00:11.063 --> 00:00:12.285
I should be at 9.

00:00:12.285 --> 00:00:15.000
This question
is the basis for the annual World Happiness Report rankings.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
According to the latest results released in March 2026,

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Taiwan’s average happiness score is 6.714,

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.000
ranking 26th in the world,

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.596
once again the highest in East Asia.

00:00:24.596 --> 00:00:26.557
How is the happiness score calculated?

00:00:26.557 --> 00:00:31.000
And where does Taiwanese people’s sense of happiness come from?

00:00:31.583 --> 00:00:32.583
What counts as happiness?

00:00:32.583 --> 00:00:34.000
The report actually only asks

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.246
the ladder question we just mentioned.

00:00:35.246 --> 00:00:37.000
It’s very simple and intuitive.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.000
how happy you feel
In other words,

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.000
is entirely based on the respondent’s subjective judgment.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.000
It doesn’t define what happiness is,

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.000
nor does it use any formulas or indicators.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Each year, more than 1,000 people are sampled in each country,

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.000
and the average of the past three years

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.246
is used to calculate the happiness score.

00:00:49.246 --> 00:00:50.000
The state of happiness

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.000
and how it is expressed

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.000
really needs to be understood

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.000
from the individual’s own perspective

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.000
to be more accurate.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:57.220
The World Happiness Report

00:00:57.233 --> 00:00:59.000
is jointly released by the United Nations, Oxford University,

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.000
and the Gallup polling organization.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Since 2012,

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.000
it has ranked countries by happiness levels.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.000
This year, 147 countries are ranked.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.000
The top five are:

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Iceland,
Finland,

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Costa Rica,
Denmark,

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.000
and Sweden.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.000
Most are Nordic countries.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.572
Finland has held the top spot

00:01:14.572 --> 00:01:16.000
for nine consecutive years since 2017.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Taiwan ranks 26th this year,

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.000
improving for three consecutive years.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.000
It ranks higher than Singapore, Japan,

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.676
China, and South Korea.

00:01:23.375 --> 00:01:24.946
Taiwan is actually pretty good.

00:01:24.946 --> 00:01:26.908
Economically, it’s quite okay.

00:01:26.908 --> 00:01:28.415
There’s probably no place more free than Taiwan.

00:01:28.415 --> 00:01:29.324
No matter good or bad,

00:01:29.324 --> 00:01:30.493
whether you like it or not,

00:01:30.493 --> 00:01:32.817
you have a space to express your thoughts.

00:01:32.817 --> 00:01:35.000
That’s what makes Taiwan great.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.000
To explain why Taiwan scores 6.7

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.000
while other countries score 5 or 7,

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.000
the report provides six additional factors

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.402
to better understand differences between countries.

00:01:43.402 --> 00:01:45.000
Four subjective factors include:

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.000
social support,

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.117
freedom to make life choices,

00:01:47.117 --> 00:01:48.234
generosity,

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:49.285
and perceptions of corruption.

00:01:49.285 --> 00:01:51.000
And two objective factors:

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.000
GDP and healthy life expectancy.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.000
The results show

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.611
that for Taiwanese people,

00:01:55.611 --> 00:01:57.000
happiness depends most on

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.000
GDP and social support.

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:00.388
Financial independence

00:02:00.388 --> 00:02:01.622
not needing to ask children for money

00:02:01.648 --> 00:02:03.000
chatting with good friends

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.000
already brings happiness.

00:02:04.311 --> 00:02:05.557
In a capitalist society,

00:02:05.557 --> 00:02:08.037
it’s not that people value money itself,

00:02:08.037 --> 00:02:10.076
but what money can provide

00:02:10.076 --> 00:02:10.792
namely,

00:02:10.792 --> 00:02:13.000
quality of life.

00:02:13.298 --> 00:02:14.648
Humans are social animals.

00:02:14.648 --> 00:02:16.000
We must live

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.507
within connections with others

00:02:18.507 --> 00:02:20.221
to feel happiness.

00:02:20.637 --> 00:02:23.000
As for how social support is defined,

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.000
the report asks respondents:

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.000
if you encounter trouble,

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.000
do you have friends or family to help?

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.454
85% of Taiwanese people said yes,

00:02:30.454 --> 00:02:32.000
ranking 61st globally.

00:02:32.233 --> 00:02:33.363
If I have difficulties,

00:02:33.363 --> 00:02:35.000
I can easily turn to family.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.311
My partner as well.

00:02:36.738 --> 00:02:37.648
Family is there,

00:02:37.648 --> 00:02:38.765
but for friends

00:02:38.765 --> 00:02:40.000
it’s harder.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.000
I don’t want to burden them,

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:44.000
so I might not share.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.415
High-quality social networks are important.

00:02:46.415 --> 00:02:47.779
When we feel wronged

00:02:47.779 --> 00:02:48.972
or need to talk,

00:02:48.972 --> 00:02:51.061
having people around us

00:02:51.061 --> 00:02:53.402
who we can truly connect with

00:02:53.402 --> 00:02:56.233
provides greater support.

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:57.337
When asked about

00:02:57.337 --> 00:02:59.596
satisfaction with freedom to choose life direction,

00:02:59.596 --> 00:03:02.000
nearly 80% of Taiwanese were satisfied,

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.000
but this ranked only 90th globally.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.000
Influenced by Confucian culture,

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.000
parents’ words are like scripture.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.000
Even though society

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.000
is becoming more open and Westernized,

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.650
encouraging individual opinions,

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:15.000
within family contexts,

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.000
especially for younger generations,

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.791
they still feel and healthy life expectancy.

00:03:18.791 --> 00:03:20.715
their freedom is restricted.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.376
But if you look at East Asia,

00:03:23.376 --> 00:03:24.637
it’s clear

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:25.533
South Korea is similar,

00:03:25.533 --> 00:03:26.533
not better than Taiwan.

00:03:26.533 --> 00:03:27.909
Japan is also the same.

00:03:27.909 --> 00:03:29.598
Happiness in East Asian societies

00:03:29.598 --> 00:03:31.181
often comes more from the collective

00:03:31.181 --> 00:03:32.506
than the individual

00:03:32.506 --> 00:03:34.506
this is called collectivism.

00:03:34.519 --> 00:03:35.946
It means your purpose in life

00:03:35.946 --> 00:03:37.946
is not just for yourself,

00:03:37.959 --> 00:03:40.350
but for a larger group.

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:43.000
I want to quickly gain the ability

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.000
to give back to my family.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.389
If my family is happy,

00:03:46.389 --> 00:03:49.116
that brings me great happiness too.

00:03:49.661 --> 00:03:51.154
Although the happiness index

00:03:51.154 --> 00:03:52.648
evaluates overall life,

00:03:52.739 --> 00:03:53.829
daily emotional states

00:03:53.829 --> 00:03:56.000
also reveal differences between countries.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.651
So the report also surveyed

00:03:57.651 --> 00:04:00.076
respondents’ positive and negative emotions

00:04:00.076 --> 00:04:01.000
from the previous day.

00:04:01.156 --> 00:04:02.933
Taiwanese people have relatively high positive emotions,

00:04:02.933 --> 00:04:04.000
ranking 34th,

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.259
and very low negative emotions,

00:04:05.259 --> 00:04:06.402
ranking 3rd lowest globally.

00:04:06.687 --> 00:04:08.323
We conducted an interesting study before.

00:04:08.323 --> 00:04:09.545
When people feel pain

00:04:09.545 --> 00:04:10.532
and go to the doctor,

00:04:10.558 --> 00:04:11.558
with 10 being very painful

00:04:11.583 --> 00:04:12.765
and 1 being no pain

00:04:12.765 --> 00:04:13.596
many Westerners rate

00:04:13.609 --> 00:04:14.350
9 or 10,

00:04:14.531 --> 00:04:16.000
while Taiwanese

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.000
give lower scores.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.000
But physiologically,

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:21.000
their condition is actually quite severe.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.000
So in expressing emotions,

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.000
Taiwanese people tend

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.000
to be more conservative.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:28.000
That’s a characteristic of Taiwanese society.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.844
What is the relationship

00:04:29.844 --> 00:04:31.000
between emotions and happiness?

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.259
Does feeling happy and joyful equal being happy overall?

00:04:33.259 --> 00:04:34.830
National Taiwan University’s Happiness Center

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:36.298
divides happiness into three dimensions:

00:04:36.298 --> 00:04:37.350
The personal dimension includes

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:38.350
mind and body,

00:04:38.376 --> 00:04:40.000
including emotional and sensory experiences.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.000
The interpersonal dimension

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.806
involves interactions with others.

00:04:43.806 --> 00:04:45.496
The environmental dimension

00:04:45.496 --> 00:04:46.952
includes external factors like stress and space.

00:04:46.952 --> 00:04:49.326
These three dimensions influence each other.

00:04:49.326 --> 00:04:50.924
The key is achieving balance.

00:04:50.924 --> 00:04:56.103
When these three are balanced,
that is what we call a state of happiness.

00:04:56.103 --> 00:04:57.337
It usually requires

00:04:57.337 --> 00:04:59.622
a longer period of time.

00:04:59.622 --> 00:05:01.000
Emotions or happiness

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.350
can change quickly,

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:05.402
but they are relatively short-term.

00:05:05.402 --> 00:05:08.402
Behind Taiwan’s top ranking in East Asia,

00:05:08.402 --> 00:05:11.286
stable economic conditions and social support are the foundation.

00:05:11.286 --> 00:05:12.000
Scholars believe

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:13.246
that psychological resilience

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:14.155
and self-awareness

00:05:14.155 --> 00:05:16.571
are what enable individuals to create happiness.

00:05:16.998 --> 00:05:18.000
A few years ago,

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.467
I experienced something unpleasant.

00:05:19.467 --> 00:05:21.000
This year I told myself

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.000
I can’t continue like this.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.000
I shouldn’t stay trapped

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.181
in those emotions.

00:05:25.246 --> 00:05:27.246
After intense negative emotions arise,

00:05:27.259 --> 00:05:29.402
it’s important to reassess

00:05:29.454 --> 00:05:31.000
and readjust.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:33.170
Adjusting how we live,

00:05:33.170 --> 00:05:34.533
adjusting our perspectives,

00:05:34.533 --> 00:05:35.754
and adjusting our emotions

00:05:35.754 --> 00:05:39.000
can lead us toward a more positive path.

